Radicale on FenrirOS
====================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled and there is no configuration,
no rights file and no users.

    cp /usr/share/doc/radicale/config.example /etc/radicale/config
    $EDITOR /etc/radicale/config
    dinitctl enable radicale

Radicale's built-in default authentication is `denyall`: nobody can log in
until you configure [auth]. For a first setup use htpasswd with bcrypt:

    [auth]
    type = htpasswd
    htpasswd_filename = /etc/radicale/users
    htpasswd_encryption = bcrypt
    [storage]
    filesystem_folder = /var/lib/radicale/collections

and create the file with `htpasswd -B -c /etc/radicale/users alice` (apache
utils) or any bcrypt-capable tool; make it readable by the radicale user.
The server listens on localhost:5232 (`hosts` in [server]); put a TLS
reverse proxy in front of it or use `ssl = True` with a certificate.
Per-collection permissions are set in the rights file
(/usr/share/doc/radicale/rights.example). Full documentation:
/usr/share/doc/radicale/DOCUMENTATION.md.
